    "guideTitle": "Welcome, Commander!",
    "guideIntro": "War Nexus is a military strategy game. Build your base, create your army, research technologies and defeat your rivals. Here are your first steps:",
    "guideStep1Title": "1. Upgrade Headquarters",
    "guideStep1Desc": "Headquarters is the foundation of all buildings and capacities. As it levels up, you can produce stronger units and store more. Always prioritize upgrading HQ.",
    "guideStep2Title": "2. Build Resource Buildings",
    "guideStep2Desc": "Oil Field, Mine, and Houses produce resources continuously. Bank earns interest on your cash. Upgrading these buildings is crucial in the long run.",
    "guideStep3Title": "3. Train Your First Soldiers",
    "guideStep3Desc": "Start producing infantry units from Barracks. Unit training requires resources and time. Each building has its own unit capacity — tied to HQ level.",
    "guideStep4Title": "4. Research",
    "guideStep4Desc": "Unlock new technologies and units from Research Lab. Each completed research gives +12% attack bonus.",
    "guideStep5Title": "5. Create Squads",
    "guideStep5Desc": "Create squads from HQ > Operations tab. You can add different unit types to a squad. You go to battle with squads.",
    "guideStep6Title": "6. Fight!",
    "guideStep6Desc": "View your rivals from Rankings and attack. You can attack players within ±5 of your rank. Win to earn resources and power.",
    "guideStep7Title": "7. Track Missions",
    "guideStep7Desc": "Complete 50 different missions from the Missions tab. Each mission rewards resources and gold. Missions guide you in the right direction.",
    "resourcesTitle": "Resources",
    "resourceCapacity": "Capacity: {{cap}}",
    "resourceSource": "Source: {{source}}",
    "resourceUsage": "Usage: {{usage}}",
    "cashSource": "Houses (production) + Bank (interest)",
    "cashUsage": "Building upgrades, unit training, research",
    "oilSource": "Oil Field",
    "oilUsage": "Building upgrades, unit training, research",
    "oreSource": "Mine",
    "oreUsage": "Building upgrades, unit training, research",
    "goldSource": "Missions + Purchase",
    "goldUsage": "Speed-ups, Bank exchange",
    "economyTipsTitle": "Economy Tips",
    "economyTip1": "• Upgrade Bank level — each level increases interest rate (+0.4%/hr/level)",
    "economyTip2": "• Upgrade resource buildings — each level increases hourly production",
    "economyTip3": "• Use Bank exchange with gold for emergency resource needs",
    "economyTip4": "• Win battles to take 20% of your rival's resources",
    "combatTitle": "Combat Rules",
    "combatRule1Title": "Cross Table",
    "combatRule1Desc": "Each unit branch has advantages/disadvantages against others. For example, infantry is weak against tanks, air defense is strong against aircraft. Check the Cross Table section for details.",
    "combatRule2Title": "Winner & Loser",
    "combatRule2Desc": "Both sides lose units equal to the opponent's unit count. The winner's advantage: resource and power transfer goes to the winner.",
    "combatRule3Title": "Resource Transfer",
    "combatRule3Desc": "After battle, 20% of the loser's resources and power are transferred to the winner.",
    "combatRule4Title": "Protection Shield",
    "combatRule4Desc": "A defending player who loses gets a 4-hour protection shield — they cannot be attacked during this time.",
    "combatRule5Title": "War Power",
    "combatRule5Desc": "warPower increases when you win and decreases when you lose. warPower cannot exceed your base power (buildings+units+research) — maximum 2x multiplier.",
    "combatRule6Title": "Player Power",
    "combatRule6Desc": "Total power = Building Power + Unit Power + Research Power + warPower (capped). This value is used for rankings.",
    "tierPowerTitle": "Unit Tier Power Values",
    "tierPower1": "• Tier 1 unit = 10 power points",
    "tierPower2": "• Tier 2 unit = 30 power points",
    "tierPower3": "• Tier 3 unit = 60 power points",
    "pvpTitle": "PvP & Rankings",
    "pvpRule1Title": "Rankings",
    "pvpRule1Desc": "All players are ranked by Player Power. Top 100 is shown. If you're below 100, you also see your region (±10).",
    "pvpRule2Title": "±5 Attack Range",
    "pvpRule2Desc": "You can only attack players 5 above and 5 below your rank. Those outside the range are shown faded.",
    "pvpRule3Title": "Cooldown (4 Hours)",
    "pvpRule3Desc": "If you attack a player and WIN, you cannot attack the same player for 4 hours. If you lose, you can attack again immediately.",
    "pvpRule4Title": "Revenge 🔥",
    "pvpRule4Desc": "If you defeat an attacker in defense, you earn revenge rights against that player. Revenge attack bypasses the ±5 rule. If you win revenge too, 4-hour cooldown starts.",
    "pvpRule5Title": "Attack Process",
    "pvpRule5Desc": "1) Choose rival from Rankings\n2) Select squad (pre-created)\n3) Press ATTACK button\n4) March timer expires\n5) Battle auto-resolves\n6) Result report shown",
    "pvpRule6Title": "Coordinate System",
    "pvpRule6Desc": "Each player has a unique coordinate in X.Y.Z format. Coordinates determine map position.",
    "squadTitle": "Squad Guide",
    "squadRule1Title": "What is a Squad?",
